---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';

const title = 'Accessibility Statement';
const description =
  'Accessibility statement for the Purinton Analytics website: WCAG 2.2 AA conformance target, measures taken in this build, and how to report barriers.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/accessibility/">
  <div class="container content-narrow">
    <Breadcrumbs
      crumbs={[
        { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
        { name: 'Accessibility', path: '/accessibility/' },
      ]}
    />
    <h1>Accessibility Statement</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Purinton Analytics wants every attorney, paralegal, and member of the public to be able
      to use this website. The site targets Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2
      Level AA, and this page describes the specific measures built into the current site
      rather than aspirational claims.
    </p>
    <p><em>This statement was prepared on August 31, 2026.</em></p>

    <h2>Measures built into this site</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Semantic HTML landmarks (header, navigation, main, footer) and a skip-to-content link on every page.</li>
      <li>A single, descriptive top-level heading per page and a logical heading order.</li>
      <li>All functionality operable by keyboard, including the mobile navigation menu, which is a real button that reports its expanded state to assistive technology.</li>
      <li>Visible focus indicators on links, buttons, and form controls.</li>
      <li>Every form field has a programmatically associated label, and validation errors are written into the field's described-by text and announced through a status region, not conveyed by color alone.</li>
      <li>No file upload controls, no time limits, and no content that flashes.</li>
      <li>Text alternatives on informative images, including the firm logo.</li>
      <li>Color combinations chosen against WCAG contrast thresholds for text on the site's navy, orange, and neutral palette.</li>
      <li>Motion and smooth scrolling are disabled for visitors whose systems request reduced motion.</li>
      <li>Responsive layout that reflows for small screens and supports browser zoom, and print stylesheets for resource checklists.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How this is checked</h2>
    <p>
      An automated test suite runs against every build of this site and verifies page
      structure, including single top-level headings, page titles and descriptions, labeled
      form fields, and working internal links. Keyboard operability and focus visibility are
      properties of the site's construction rather than afterthoughts: navigation, menus, and
      forms use native links, buttons, and form controls that carry the browser's standard
      keyboard behavior, with a shared visible focus style.
    </p>

    <h2>Known limitations</h2>
    <p>
      No unresolved accessibility barriers are known at the date of this statement. External
      websites linked from this site, including government data sources, are outside the
      firm's control.
    </p>

    <h2>Feedback and alternate formats</h2>
    <p>
      If any part of this site is difficult to use with your assistive technology, or if you
      need any content in an alternate format, contact
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or call
      <a href={`tel:${SITE.phoneE164}`}>{SITE.phoneDisplay}</a>. Please describe the page and
      the barrier you encountered; reported issues are reviewed and addressed.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
